  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset titled \"How to edit a manuscript on GitHub with Manubot\" supports the Sustainable Development Goal of Quality Education and has had at least one instance of reuse in an academic context. While it has garnered minimal visibility, with just three total views, its open access provides foundational resources for those interested in utilizing GitHub for manuscript editing.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Released in 2019 on Figshare, the dataset explores the practical aspects of using GitHub alongside Manubot for manuscript editing. Despite its utility in promoting open-source collaboration and enhancing documentation practices, it has yet to attract significant attention, evidenced by the absence of citations and mentions in broader academic discourse.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The work is framed within key areas of computer science, software development, and open-source methodologies, reinforcing its relevance in improving scholarly communication practices. The research aligns notably with the Sustainable Development Goals, particularly emphasizing Quality Education, which indicates its potential influence in educational contexts.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset has been reused once, highlighting its role in advancing biomedical research. Such reuse underscores the relevance of the methodologies discussed in the original work and affirms the dataset's value as a resource for similar projects. The authorship includes David Slochower and Daniel Himmelstein, with the latter associated with a distinctive ORCID identifier.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Access to the dataset remains open, facilitating a broad audience\u2019s engagement. Future efforts to promote awareness and application of this work may help enhance its impact within the scholarly community, particularly as researchers increasingly seek effective and collaborative tools for manuscript preparation and editing.</p>",
